<bold>Figure S2A.</bold> Treatment patterns of non&#x02010;metastatic prostate cancer (nmPC) in the data lake cohort. Of all nmPC patients in this cohort. 75% (n&#x02009;=&#x02009;4761) received at least some PC specific treatment.</p><p>
<bold>Figure S2B.</bold> Treatment patterns of metastatic prostate cancer (mPC) in the data lake cohort. Of all mPC patients in this cohort. 99% (n&#x02009;=&#x02009;2373) received at least some PC specific treatment.</p></caption><media xlink:href="BCO2-6-e70098-s001.docx"/></supplementary-material></sec></body><back><ack id="bco270098-sec-0022"><title>ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS</title><p>The authors have nothing to report.</p></ack><sec sec-type="data-availability" id="bco270098-sec-0019"><title>DATA AVAILABILITY STATEMENT</title><p>The data are not publicly available but require the permission of the Finnish Social and Health Data Permit Authority.</p></sec><ref-list id="bco270098-bibl-0001" content-type="cited-references"><title>REFERENCES</title><ref id="bco270098-bib-0001"><label>1</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal" id="bco270098-cit-0002">
